        {
            "_id": "BvW0oiNlKIAxOPrr",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Three-Headed",
            "sort": 500000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "defensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>Any ability that would sever a greater chimera's head (such as a critical hit with a @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.equipment-srd.Item.Vorpal] weapon) severs one head at random. Losing a head doesn't kill a chimera (as long as it has at least one head left), but it does prevent it from making Strikes with the lost head or using any abilities granted by the head.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": []
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "M8CbYRKihCNDpNGI",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Fire Breath",
            "sort": 600000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>Doomcrier's magma worm head exhales a blast of flame in a @Template[type:cone|distance:30] that deals @Damage[16d6[fire]|options:area-damage] damage to all creatures in the area (@Check[reflex|dc:36|basic|options:area-effect] save). It can't use Fire Breath again for [[/gmr 1d4 #Recharge Fire Breath]]{1d4 rounds}.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "fire",
                        "primal"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "hRb6Mcq25HBNlBQG",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Multiple Reactions",
            "sort": 700000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>A greater chimera gains 2 extra reactions each round that it can use only to make Reactive Strikes. It must use a different head for each reaction, and it can't use more than one on the same triggering action. If it loses one of its heads, it also loses one of these extra reactions.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": []
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "kixUx73oj09Sr7fh",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Storm Blast",
            "sort": 800000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>Doomcrier's thunderbird head blasts its foes with peals of thunder and crackling bolts of lightning. Each creature in a @Template[type:emanation|distance:30] takes @Damage[8d6[electricity],8d6[sonic]|options:area-damage] damage (@Check[reflex|dc:36|basic] save). Doomcrier can't use Lightning Blast for [[/gmr 1d4 #rounds]]{1d4 rounds}.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": [
                        "primal"
                    ]
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "ipu2uvrrUMZRvNwP",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/default-icons/action.svg",
            "name": "Three-Headed Strike",
            "sort": 900000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "action"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": 2
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>The greater chimera makes a Strike with each of its heads, each at a –2 penalty and targeting a different creature. These Strikes count as only one attack for the greater chimera's multiple attack penalty, and the penalty doesn't increase until after it has made all three attacks.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [
                    {
                        "key": "RollOption",
                        "option": "three-head-strike",
                        "toggleable": true
                    },
                    {
                        "key": "FlatModifier",
                        "predicate": [
                            "three-head-strike"
                        ],
